"""Student-facing structure shared by the notebook builder and retained notebook."""
import nbformat as nbf
INTRO = '## Start here: two parts, one new function\n\n**Your goal:** first run a worked example that checks velocity derivatives; then\nuse a coding assistant to add **one new function**, `net_volume_flux(x, y, u, v)`.\nYou are not building another cavity solver or training an AI model.\n\n**Before starting:** know Python arrays, the velocity components u and v, and basic\nderivatives and integrals. Use Colab or a local Python checkout. For the assessed\npart, use any accessible coding assistant and a GitHub fork. Ask the instructor\nfor an alternative if you cannot access an assistant.\n\n| Part | What you do | What counts as completion |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| A: worked example | Run the supplied cells without editing the solver; interpret the analytic and cavity checks | Explain the grid-error trend and why the deliberate wrong-axis candidate fails |\n| B: your contribution | Specify, implement, test and review the boundary-flux function | Submit the new code, tests and evidence listed in ASSIGNMENT.md |\n\n**File guide:** `SCIENTIFIC_SPEC.md` describes the completed derivative example.\n`SPEC.md` is the template YOU complete for the new flux function. They describe\ndifferent quantities. Run all executes the demonstration; it does not complete Part B.\n\n**Six steps:** (1) run Part A; (2) predict the flux examples below by hand;\n(3) complete and commit your specification; (4) request and save the first agent\npatch; (5) run tests, review and correct; (6) submit your evidence and final diff.\n\n### The physical picture for Part B\nVelocity crosses four edges of a rectangle. Outward flow is positive:\n\\[\nQ=\\int_{y_{min}}^{y_{max}}[u(y,x_{max})-u(y,x_{min})]dy\n+\\int_{x_{min}}^{x_{max}}[v(y_{max},x)-v(y_{min},x)]dx.\n\\]\nArrays use `u[j,i] = u(y[j],x[i])`. Integrate using supplied coordinates and\ncomposite trapezoids. Q has units of area/time (volume flow per unit depth).\nConstant velocity gives Q=0. On the unit square, u=x and v=y give Q=2.\nA zero total can hide locally incorrect flow: Q is global balance, whereas\ndivergence checks local balance.\n\n### Part A: predict, run, explain\nBefore each result, write your prediction. After the grid study, explain whether\nhalving spacing roughly quarters the error. After the cavity check, explain why\nsmall divergence alone does not prove physical accuracy. After the deliberately\nfaulty candidate, identify the wrong derivative axis: rejection is the expected\nsuccessful outcome of that test.\n'
WORKSPACE = '## Part B: your student workspace\n\nStop before asking an agent: complete and commit your own SPEC.md first.\nThen save the first generated candidate as `flowmllab/student_mass_balance.py`;\ndo not overwrite instructor modules. Add your own tests in a new test file.\nThe cell below checks your saved candidate when you deliberately enable it.\nIt does not generate the solution. Copy evidence logs before rerunning if you\nneed to retain a failed attempt. Colab storage is temporary: save your notebook,\nexport your files and commit the evidence to your own fork before disconnecting.\n\n**Your written answers:** (1) Which edge carries each minus sign, and why?\n(2) Derive Q for u=x, v=y before testing. (3) Give a field with zero total flux\nbut nonzero local divergence. (4) Which test would reject a function that always\nreturns zero? (5) What did you personally change or verify in the agent patch?\n'

def improve_cells(cells):
    if any(c.get("id") == "student-roadmap" for c in cells):
        return cells
    cells.insert(1, nbf.v4.new_markdown_cell(INTRO, id="student-roadmap"))
    for c in cells:
        if c.cell_type == "markdown":
            for name in ["ASSIGNMENT.md", "SPEC.md", "SCIENTIFIC_SPEC.md", "LINE_REVIEW.md", "PROCESS_LOG.md", "REPORT.md"]:
                c.source = c.source.replace("](" + name + ")", "](https://github.com/Ehsan-Roohi/FlowMLLab/blob/main/notebooks/week01_1/" + name + ")")
    cells.extend([nbf.v4.new_markdown_cell(WORKSPACE, id="student-workspace"),
        nbf.v4.new_code_cell('# Part B: run only AFTER your specification-first commit and candidate are saved.\nRUN_STUDENT_CHECKS = False\nif RUN_STUDENT_CHECKS:\n    candidate = ROOT / "flowmllab/student_mass_balance.py"\n    if not candidate.is_file():\n        raise FileNotFoundError("Save your agent candidate at " + str(candidate))\n    commands = [[sys.executable, "qa/check_week01_1_candidate.py", str(candidate)],\n                [sys.executable, "-m", "unittest", "tests.test_scientific_software", "-v"]]\n    evidence = ROOT / "submissions/week01_1/evidence"\n    evidence.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    for i, command in enumerate(commands, 1):\n        run = subprocess.run(command, cwd=ROOT, text=True, capture_output=True)\n        log = run.stdout + run.stderr + "\\nEXIT CODE: " + str(run.returncode)\n        (evidence / f"check_{i}.txt").write_text(log, encoding="utf-8")\n        print(log)\n', id="student-checks")])
    return cells
